Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-02-2001||03:38 AM||||Im curious...if you were going to go through all the motions of removing the engine in the car, why would you put another 4 banger in it? Im not bashing 4 bangers, I like 'em...but I would think that if you were to go through all the trouble of removing an engine and reinstalling one, you'd go w/ a 6 or an 8. Seems like an aweful lot of work for another 4 banger, regardless of what kind of 4 banger it is. Just courious.........<BR>(BTW, I believe that Standards car used to be Pherders....ask him about all the "fun" he had installing that engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||10-02-2001||02:02 PM||||Yeah, paul said he had the engine in and out of the car.. what, 16 times?  The swap is going to be just as much trouble as a 3800 or SBC.  <P>The advantages are the lighter weight, and 30 mpg.  Off the line it's no faster than a stock v6, but on the highway is where it really shines.<P>If you are going to swap a quad 4 in, make sure it's an HO.  Anything else is not worth it.  And don't get a '95 quad 4, transition year where they added balance shafts to the 2.3, which drops it to 150 hp.  <P>Why go with the quad?  6800 rpm redline, 180hp and 165lb/ft of torque.  Somewhat decent aftermarket, mainly through  <A HREF="http://www.mantapart.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mantaparts.com</A>  and RK Sport.  Mantapart does have some cool stuff, like solid lifters.  9,000 rpm redline hehehee   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> <P>If I ever get around to doing an engine swap, I'm not going to do a quad 4.  Most likely a 3800 or v8.  The thing that sucks about having a quad 4 is most people think Fiero's came with them stock... so you pop the decklid and most people are just like "oh" grrr   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>oh yeah.. I've calculated the E.T for the coupe to be mid-low 14's.  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 10-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||87FieroGTx||10-02-2001||04:28 PM|||| You can turbo Q4's up to 325hp! They make great AutoX engines but for the street/drags I would go 3800s/c.||||reg||4
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||10-02-2001||04:41 PM||||My thoughts exactly ..an 88 coupe with a Q4 would be a killer autocross car.<P>the lighter the better.<P>JM ||||reg||1
